# Gate step 1461-5rm6 — data, not code (order 1072-b7eq).
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS. scripts/land-queue.sh resolved tillandsias-plan relative to
# the CALLER's cwd, so a run from anywhere but a checkout with target/ found no
# binary. Its fixture calls it from scratch repos, and under the darwin gate
# regime (TILLANDSIAS_PLAN_BIN and CARGO_TARGET_DIR unset) it failed 12/14;
# Linux hid it because CARGO_TARGET_DIR resolves from anywhere. Bound so the
# fixed resolver cannot regress unseen (the same bug recurred three times on
# 2026-09-28). About 10 s, gh stubbed, no network.
#
# 2398-zvug: scripts/test-land-queue.sh became three Lua fixtures split by arm
# group; this step runs arms 1-13 (landing), steps 291 and 293 the other two.
#
# STEP_LUA is a LITERAL path on purpose (1063-nraf).
STEP_DESC="Checking the land queue orders, evicts and re-queues, resolving its plan binary from its own root (1461-5rm6, arms 1-13)"
STEP_LUA="scripts/lua/test-land-queue-landing.lua"
STEP_ERROR="the land queue fixture failed; if every arm reads no-plan-binary, land-queue.sh again resolves tillandsias-plan from the caller's cwd (1461-5rm6)"
STEP_OK="land queue behaves, with its plan binary resolved from its own checkout"
# 1553-x8js: the previous darwin record, "tlatoanis-macbook-air 2026-09-28
# darwin ok:land-queue:16/16", was INVALID for ARM 9 — BSD sed never built the
# stdin-hungry gh stub, so ARM 9 passed vacuously (it passed even against a
# land-queue.sh with the fd-3 read reverted). Re-measured 2026-10-08 with the
# stub built and checked; ARM 9 now reds against that revert.
STEP_SECOND_REGIME="tlatoanis-macbook-air 2026-11-26 darwin ok:land-queue-landing:25 arms at 1d37addfb (relayed by macbookair)"
# ORDER 2155-gpar: runs alone, never beside a sibling step in the gate pool.
STEP_SERIAL="watches the shared timing or metrics log, or runs a nested gate"
STEP_LANES="timing"
# ORDER 2157-ginp: STEP_READS, the paths this step reads, RECORDED ONLY: never
# consulted by the class-selector skip (that is STEP_INPUTS, 2118-tnut). First
# cut: the step's own script plus every repo path it names literally.
STEP_READS="crates/tillandsias-macos-tray/** crates/tillandsias-macos-tray/src/** methodology/convergence.yaml plan/index.d/** scripts/land-queue.sh lib/lua/common/land_queue_fixture.lua scripts/lua/test-land-queue-landing.lua"
